<description>&lt;p&gt;Armed clashes and intercommunal violence persist in South Sudan, with rebel and SPLA-IO forces attacking civilians in Tonj East, Warrap State and Greater Pibor, while worshippers were attacked in Gorom refugee camp and a teen was killed for refusing an arranged marriage. UNMISS is supporting deterrence efforts in Tonj East and calling for stronger civilian protection during a visit to Unity, and the Gender Ministry has raised concerns about violence against women and children ahead of a 16 Days campaign. President Kiir told an Oil and Power conference that partnerships, not speeches, must change lives, after travelling to Ethiopia and holding investment talks with Saudi Arabia in Riyadh. A US senator warned that Uganda is playing a destabilising role, the Crisis Group urged African intervention, and the UNDP resident representative issued a message of solidarity. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTFBOTF9pY0NmbXA5N0JTUTJpSl9mdEY4aDExN3hPeENmbUVHRW5NVEpERGxidERUbEVCMWE3LUlPRVdiY1hHa0FLUGxiblhMUk9tQkY1aU04bXdtam0wd2dCMHdJazZHLVpsSER6UURucjMtSXlBTkE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Mail &amp;amp; Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxPMXNMeVJ1MnEwUVJUa0ZIdnpzN05nVnNFYVpmeE0wZ2QzZktQbTR6Vmp4dncwOGpqeEhhTEg4TWoxNXd0TXRCTTQzaE9RVGJEUG1NZkM0VnU5TlZ3TU5aem9wUXF5djZTWGI2WFlmbHozMFVLck9jb3NlNUJmdzMtVkJWVm5sbUFKdTR0bzlDNTh6eU9saWppc2E0UVluS1J2MEFuVFpFZEJLLUZZMkhOeFJsVnZkY0hSVVJnNnJfaHRxeXNLYlN2Vw?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxNQ25NdTZBY0FvSjFzMlB1b1ZEcFZISzY4ajh2aE9vcDJObUdRcldoa2w1UTJ5clNaT1VwZjlNaHhrTzB3TXBCR1piWVptSXJNOVRNZWZDMU9oSmh3NmUzbkZjVDNSV1JiRjgyS2YxM2lXYlBiek9WXzlrRkIxSlljY2JPeTNMaml6QzdUcUQtaExqb3ZPY1llQ0xMb